    "text": "<p>Consider the following complex ions</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>FeF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>–</mo></mrow></msup></math>,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mo>[</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>)</mo><msub><mo> </mo><mn>6</mn></msub><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo> </mo><mo>=</mo><mo> </mo><mo>[</mo><mi>Fe</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>6</mn></msub><msup><mo>]</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math></p><p>The correct order of the complex ions, according to their spin only magnetic moment values (in B.M.) is :</p>"
